{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZCorner","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.corner_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.corner_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L139-L186","doc":"**Asymptotic uniqueness at a normal-crossing corner.** If two normalised germs\n`F₁, F₂` (holomorphic in each variable at the corner, `F(0,0) = 1`) satisfy\n`F₁(α,β) α^X β^Y = F₂(α,β) α^X β^Y K` on a real quadrant `(0, δ)²`, then `K = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.gauge_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.gauge_const","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L76-L137","doc":"**One-variable asymptotic uniqueness.** A germ `U` holomorphic at `0` which equals\n`t^X C t^{−X}` along a real segment `(0, δ)` is the constant `C`, and `C` commutes with `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.analyticAt_inverse_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.analyticAt_inverse_mul","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L69-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.ofReal_mem_ball","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.ofReal_mem_ball","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L65-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.hasDerivAt_comp_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.hasDerivAt_comp_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L58-L63","doc":"Restriction of a complex derivative to the real line, for `R`-valued maps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.hasDerivAt_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.hasDerivAt_conj","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L46-L55","doc":"`z ↦ z^X C z^{−X}` satisfies `z Φ' = [X, Φ]` on the slit plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.commute_cpowA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.commute_cpowA","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L43-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.cpowA_neg_mul_cpowA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.cpowA_neg_mul_cpowA","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L39-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZCorner.cpowA_mul_cpowA_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZCorner.cpowA_mul_cpowA_neg","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZCorner.lean#L34-L37","signatureChunk":0}]}